  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Provençal market on Place des Lices, in the heart of Saint-Tropez, takes place every Tuesday and Saturday morning, from 8am to 1pm, all year round. You will find food, textiles, decor, crafts and souvenirs, in the shade of the square's centuries-old plane trees.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The market and square pages on the Saint-Tropez Tourisme website mention no rule on the presence of dogs (neither permission nor ban). However, the English version of the market page relayed by the Le Lavandou tourist office says "No pets". As the market can be very busy at peak times, if you come with your dog, keep it close to you on a short leash, follow the signs displayed on site and check with the Saint-Tropez tourist office (04 94 97 45 21) before you come.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the tourist office advises arriving at opening time, before the late-morning crowds, which is also more comfortable for a dog.</div>

      <h2>Practical information</h2>
      <p>Access to the market is free. According to the square's page on the tourist office website, public toilets and a car park nearby are mentioned; the square itself is open all year round, every day. To avoid traffic jams, the tourist office advises arriving early, ideally before 8:30am, or coming by sea shuttle from Sainte-Maxime or Saint-Raphaël, by ZOU! network buses or by bike. Products vary with the season (fruit and vegetables, crafts, textiles, plants and flowers).</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The port of Saint-Tropez and its cobbled lanes are a few steps from the square. The Place aux Herbes also hosts a market of fish and fresh produce (fruit, vegetables, flowers). Outside market days, Place des Lices remains a lively place open every day, popular with pétanque players.</p>
    </div>

